welcome:
Welcome to the Engineering Team at Nkwen Traders.

Let me tell you where we are. We have four shops: Nkwen, Mile 4, Commercial Avenue and our new branch in Bafoussam. Customers phone to ask if rice is in stock. Prices change every week, and the new list travels on paper. Our sales reps write wholesale orders in notebooks. **We need software, and we need people who can build it well. That is why you are here.**

Here is what you will build with us:

- our website, easy to read on any phone, even on slow data;
- a catalogue where customers search, filter and fill a basket;
- the live product list, loaded from our own API;
- then, in your pathway, the real systems: our APIs for orders, stock and mobile money, the React shop, or our reps' app;
- and finally, with a squad, the orders platform the whole company will use.

I will be honest with you. I will ask a lot. Tests that pass. Work on time. Every line explained, including the lines an AI tool helped you write. Code that our cashiers and customers can trust with their money.

But hear this. Every senior engineer you admire started exactly where you are today: unsure, a little scared, fighting their first error message. What made them senior was not talent. It was **thousands of small problems solved, tested and explained, one week after another.** Bugs the morning after a release. Code reviews. Failed payments. Deadlines. Interviews. In this track you meet all of them, in safe doses, with Ms. Lum Nadine and the team beside you.

Your part is simple, but not easy: **show up every week, ship your work, explain it, and ask when you are stuck.**

This orientation shows you the whole road: what the job really is, how far it can take you, and where this program leaves you. Take your time. Then let's build.
